{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792417832496,"sessionID":"ses_eab9286adffefIgH30nghYVaCI","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call-0cff88fe-93f9-44a4-8390-c6f2891ed2cf-2","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-19\\40-critique.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-19\\40-critique.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Critique - 2026-10-19\n2: \n3: ## Scores\n4: \n5: | variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n6: |---------|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|-------|--------|\n7: | a       | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16    | no |\n8: \n9: b and c were not built. The brief said to try them only if the shared scale read as the swim card or hid the slow station. It does neither.\n10: \n11: ## What each variant gets right / wrong\n12: \n13: ### Variant a (shared scale)\n14: \n15: Right: landscape, portrait, square and the tutorial all exit 0 with `degraded: false`. `stills/square.png` shows `1:11:40` as the largest figure, `#64`, and eight named rows; lap 4 fills the rail and its burpee bar is longer than the run; lap 6 is the short tape and the carry bar is the short accent. Portrait and square stay one stack, one line per row (`Burpee`, `1:52`, `240` all fit). Footer on every still is `6:06` / `36:20` / `4:20`. No `HYROX`, no `SkiErg`, no yellow lockup. Tests assert the 386/584 bar rule, the checksum, fail-fast field names, and bindings (24 split paths). `check-registry` is clean for this id.\n16: \n17: Wrong: the place column on `stills/landscape.png` is a bare `42`..`240` with no header, so a stranger cannot tell those are station places. `tutorial-2.png` quotes PacePost and Sweatlas and lists the four sources the scout opened, but glues \"That card stops at the finish\" onto the Sweatlas quote and paraphrases Rox Lyfe. `tutorial-6.png` shows scout and plan with numbers that match those trace rows, and omits build (114 calls, 7.8M tokens, $4.66, 23 min), so the headline \"2 phases / $1.48\" is not the day. Ship is supposed to refresh that page; it is not a feature the card claims, so it is not fatal.\n18: \n19: ## Decision: SHIP a\n20: \n21: ## If ship: what a human polish pass should look at first\n22: \n23: The place column. On every still the right-hand numbers have no label, and `240` next to Burpee reads as an unexplained count. A `PLC` header, only if it still fits at 480x270, is the first pixel fix. Second: on `stills/landscape.png` the `RANK` label sits on the header rule; give it a few pixels. Before publish, copy `trace.json` into `WHY.timeline` or tutorial-6 will ship a day that never mentions the build.\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Critique - 2026-10-19\n\n## Scores\n\n| variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n|---------|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|-------|--------|\n| a       | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16    | no |\n\nb and c were not built. The brief said to try them only if the shared scale read as the swim card or hid the slow station. It does neither.\n\n## What each variant gets right / wrong\n\n### Variant a (shared scale)\n\nRight: landscape, portrait, square and the tutorial all exit 0 with `degraded: false`. `stills/square.png` shows `1:11:40` as the largest figure, `#64`, and eight named rows; lap 4 fills the rail and its burpee bar is longer than the run; lap 6 is the short tape and the carry bar is the short accent. Portrait and square stay one stack, one line per row (`Burpee`, `1:52`, `240` all fit). Footer on every still is `6:06` / `36:20` / `4:20`. No `HYROX`, no `SkiErg`, no yellow lockup. Tests assert the 386/584 bar rule, the checksum, fail-fast field names, and bindings (24 split paths). `check-registry` is clean for this id.\n\nWrong: the place column on `stills/landscape.png` is a bare `42`..`240` with no header, so a stranger cannot tell those are station places. `tutorial-2.png` quotes PacePost and Sweatlas and lists the four sources the scout opened, but glues \"That card stops at the finish\" onto the Sweatlas quote and paraphrases Rox Lyfe. `tutorial-6.png` shows scout and plan with numbers that match those trace rows, and omits build (114 calls, 7.8M tokens, $4.66, 23 min), so the headline \"2 phases / $1.48\" is not the day. Ship is supposed to refresh that page; it is not a feature the card claims, so it is not fatal.\n\n## Decision: SHIP a\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-19\\40-critique.md","text":"# Critique - 2026-10-19\n\n## Scores\n\n| variant | 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 | total | fatal? |\n|---------|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|-------|--------|\n| a       | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 16    | no |\n\nb and c were not built. The brief said to try them only if the shared scale read as the swim card or hid the slow station. It does neither.\n\n## What each variant gets right / wrong\n\n### Variant a (shared scale)\n\nRight: landscape, portrait, square and the tutorial all exit 0 with `degraded: false`. `stills/square.png` shows `1:11:40` as the largest figure, `#64`, and eight named rows; lap 4 fills the rail and its burpee bar is longer than the run; lap 6 is the short tape and the carry bar is the short accent. Portrait and square stay one stack, one line per row (`Burpee`, `1:52`, `240` all fit). Footer on every still is `6:06` / `36:20` / `4:20`. No `HYROX`, no `SkiErg`, no yellow lockup. Tests assert the 386/584 bar rule, the checksum, fail-fast field names, and bindings (24 split paths). `check-registry` is clean for this id.\n\nWrong: the place column on `stills/landscape.png` is a bare `42`..`240` with no header, so a stranger cannot tell those are station places. `tutorial-2.png` quotes PacePost and Sweatlas and lists the four sources the scout opened, but glues \"That card stops at the finish\" onto the Sweatlas quote and paraphrases Rox Lyfe. `tutorial-6.png` shows scout and plan with numbers that match those trace rows, and omits build (114 calls, 7.8M tokens, $4.66, 23 min), so the headline \"2 phases / $1.48\" is not the day. Ship is supposed to refresh that page; it is not a feature the card claims, so it is not fatal.\n\n## Decision: SHIP a\n\n## If ship: what a human polish pass should look at first\n\nThe place column. On every still the right-hand numbers have no label, and `240` next to Burpee reads as an unexplained count. A `PLC` header, only if it still fits at 480x270, is the first pixel fix. Second: on `stills/landscape.png` the `RANK` label sits on the header rule; give it a few pixels. Before publish, copy `trace.json` into `WHY.timeline` or tutorial-6 will ship a day that never mentions the build.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":23,"totalLines":23,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-19\\40-critique.md","time":{"start":1792417832411,"end":1792417832470}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_50591150-4be2-93af-b9c1-05cc448195bb_2"}},"id":"prt_1546d9dcf001FKN6pY2G25QGpD","sessionID":"ses_eab9286adffefIgH30nghYVaCI","messageID":"msg_1546d7b2c001ofTM6q13yqAFLM"}}
