{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792417919734,"sessionID":"ses_eab9286adffefIgH30nghYVaCI","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call-a4f41d84-b81e-4f33-861f-922a2071fe0a-25","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\tools\\gen-previews.mjs","limit":80},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\tools\\gen-previews.mjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: /**\n3:  * Mint preview assets for the Templates-page browse cards (founder-run; not CI).\n4:  *\n5:  * For every manifest entry without a preview image (or with --force), renders\n6:  *   assets/templates/<templateKey with \"/\" -> \"__\">/preview.png\n7:  * via the m0saic CLI at 1920x1080. Ids listed in ANIMATED_PREVIEW_IDS also get\n8:  * preview.mp4 (1920x1080, the template's own length) + poster.png.\n9:  *\n10:  * Every VIDEO template also gets preview.gif: a short loop of its clip at its\n11:  * defaults, for the directory page (TEMPLATES.md) - GitHub plays a GIF inline\n12:  * and will not play a repo .mp4. The clip is rendered once at 640x360 (or the\n13:  * committed preview.mp4 is reused), sped up when it is longer than ten\n14:  * seconds so the whole clip fits the loop, and encoded by ffmpeg with its own\n15:  * palette. The manifest does not list it (hosts use image / video / poster);\n16:  * tools/gen-gallery.mjs finds it by name. A GIF that cannot be minted is a\n17:  * warning, never a failure: the browse card is the still, and a day does not\n18:  * fail over a directory thumbnail.\n19:  *\n20:  * Budgets (SOFT, 2026-09-14): preview.png > 500 KB or preview.mp4 > 5 MB prints a\n21:  * warning and keeps the file — devs want previews that look like the product, not\n22:  * 360p thumbnails. Trim the default props only when a warning says so.\n23:  * preview.gif > 3 MB warns the same way.\n24:  *\n25:  * CLI resolution and Windows quoting: same rules as tools/smoke-render.mjs\n26:  * (M0SAIC_CLI env override,