ts it (\"Image outputs are not supported for mosaic_pipeline\n69:  *      renderables under emit:single\").\n70:  *   2. The template renders fine as an image, but the FIRST FRAME is not\n71:  *      representative — a timed sequence has barely started at t=0, and any\n72:  *      reveal that begins from nothing is outright blank there.\n73:  *\n74:  *  Needs an ffmpeg on PATH (or M0SAIC_FFMPEG), same as\n75:  *  tools/regen-fixtures.mjs. */\n76: const STILL_FROM_VIDEO = new Set([\n77:   // (2) the front door: the field wipes in and the M assembles — t=0 is a\n78:   // bare navy canvas; the card is settled only at the end of the clip.\n79:   \"@one-a-day/basics/hello-world/v1\",\n80: ]);\n\n(Showing lines 1-80 of 337. Use offset=81 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n/**\n * Mint preview assets for the Templates-page browse cards (founder-run; not CI).\n *\n * For every manifest entry without a preview image (or with --force), renders\n *   assets/templates/<templateKey with \"/\" -> \"__\">/preview.png\n * via the m0saic CLI at 1920x1080. Ids listed in ANIMATED_PREVIEW_IDS also get\n * preview.mp4 (1920x1080, the template's own length) + poster.png.\n *\n * Every VIDEO template also gets preview.gif: a short loop of its clip at its\n * defaults, for the directory page (TEMPLATES.md) - GitHub plays a GIF inline\n * and will not play a repo .mp4. The clip is rendered once at 640x360 (or the\n * committed preview.mp4 is reused), sped up when it is longer than ten\n * seconds so the whole clip fits the loop, and encoded by ffmpeg with its own\n * palette. The manifest does not list it (hosts use image / video / poster);\n * tools/gen-gallery.mjs finds it by name. A GIF that cannot be minted is a\n * warning, never a failure: the browse card is the still, and a day does not\n * fail over a directory thumbnail.\n *\n * Budgets (SOFT, 2026-09-14): preview.png > 500 KB or preview.mp4 > 5 MB prints a","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display"